WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.152 --> 00:00:17.585
Mr. helped Josh and me make three coloring machines.

2
00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:20.968
Josh's little sister, Jenny, helped too.

3
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.911
So did their dog, Bunch.

4
00:00:27.773 --> 00:00:30.636
He picked up all the pieces of wood we dropped on the floor.

5
00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:34.310
"This is the best invention in the world!"

6
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:35.611
Josh told me.

7
00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:38.613
Josh always says things like that.

8
00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:41.115
He's the best friend in the world.

9
00:00:41.135 --> 00:00:47.840
"I sure hope these coloring machines work," said Jenny, sneezing.

10
00:00:49.061 --> 00:00:53.685
Everything makes Jenny sneeze, especially wood scraps and dust.

11
00:00:54.685 --> 00:00:57.848
Even Josh's hamster, Sparky, makes Jenny sneeze.

12
00:00:59.356 --> 00:01:02.999
"I'm going to bring the coloring machines to school tomorrow," I said.

13
00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:06.281
"Wait until the other kids see them!"

14
00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:09.883
"You'll be the most famous kid in school!"

15
00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:11.004
said Josh.

16
00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.086
"Ah-choo!" Jenny sneezed.

17
00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:19.490
The next day I took my coloring machines to school with me.

18
00:01:20.631 --> 00:01:23.773
Mrs. Romano was very impressed with my invention.

19
00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:26.675
"What a creative idea, Iggy!"

20
00:01:27.115 --> 00:01:27.596
she said.

21
00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.550
"Our hands will never get tired from coloring again!"

22
00:01:32.031 --> 00:01:32.691
said Jake.

23
00:01:33.772 --> 00:01:36.975
"Even when we have to color Asia," said Ruby.

24
00:01:38.136 --> 00:01:42.439
Everyone laughed, remembering how long it had taken to color Asia.

25
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.504
Molly, Ruby, and Evan volunteered to try out my new invention.

26
00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:53.969
I showed them how to tape their crayons inside the round part of the machine.

27
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:58.777
"Move the machine around so the crayon colors," I explained.

28
00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:01.739
"Let the machine do all the work!"

29
00:02:03.561 --> 00:02:06.143
Evan started filling in North America with blue.

30
00:02:06.163 --> 00:02:13.329
"This is really hard, Iggy," he said as he moved the automatic coloring machine around.

31
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.430
Ruby frowned.

32
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.353
"It's even harder than coloring by hand!"

33
00:02:18.373 --> 00:02:23.617
"Well, at least your hand doesn't get tired," I pointed out.

34
00:02:23.637 --> 00:02:28.385
"Look, my crayon broke!"

35
00:02:28.865 --> 00:02:30.185
Ruby said with dismay.

36
00:02:30.205 --> 00:02:32.686
"Mine did too!"

37
00:02:33.207 --> 00:02:33.867
said Evan.

38
00:02:35.728 --> 00:02:36.708
Molly looked at me.

39
00:02:36.728 --> 00:02:40.810
"Iggy, this is a brilliant invention," she said.

40
00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.311
I grinned proudly.

41
00:02:44.251 --> 00:02:46.692
"Really?" "Yes," said Molly.

42
00:02:46.712 --> 00:02:49.473
"But there's only one problem."

43
00:02:49.493 --> 00:02:51.414
"What's that?"

44
00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:52.254
I asked.

45
00:02:52.274 --> 00:02:54.915
"It doesn't work!"

46
00:02:55.436 --> 00:02:56.096
said Molly.

47
00:02:57.264 --> 00:02:58.545
I hated to admit it.

48
00:02:59.405 --> 00:03:00.786
But Molly was right.

49
00:03:02.286 --> 00:03:06.228
That day when I got home from school, I felt really bad.

50
00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:10.230
My coloring machine was a big failure.

51
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.472
I threw the machines in the back of my bedroom closet.

52
00:03:15.252 --> 00:03:17.253
I didn't want to ever see them again.

53
00:03:17.273 --> 00:03:22.915
"Mom! Iggy threw his invention junk in my half of the closet!"

54
00:03:23.196 --> 00:03:23.956
yelled Tate.

55
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.302
"Boys, please be quiet!"

56
00:03:27.702 --> 00:03:28.422
called Mom.

57
00:03:28.442 --> 00:03:30.804
"I'm talking on the telephone!"

58
00:03:33.226 --> 00:03:35.167
I lay down on my bed to think.

59
00:03:36.809 --> 00:03:41.572
I wished I could think of a really wonderful new invention—one that actually worked.

60
00:03:43.393 --> 00:03:45.215
There was a knock on the apartment door.

61
00:03:46.376 --> 00:03:47.116
It was Molly.

62
00:03:47.136 --> 00:03:50.899
"Iggy, Caswell has disappeared again!"

63
00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:52.000
she cried.

64
00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.333
Caswell is Molly's little brother.

65
00:03:56.673 --> 00:03:59.694
He loves to go exploring in our old apartment building.

66
00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:05.075
He likes to look for hidden treasure, but sometimes he gets lost.

67
00:04:07.996 --> 00:04:09.536
Once we found him in the basement.

68
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:12.757
Another time we found him on the roof.

69
00:04:13.938 --> 00:04:16.798
I couldn't imagine who would hide a treasure on the roof!

70
00:04:18.059 --> 00:04:22.280
Everyone helped look for Caswell, except for Mom, who was still on the phone.

71
00:04:23.712 --> 00:04:26.254
"Caswell, where are you?"

72
00:04:26.835 --> 00:04:27.415
we called.

73
00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.221
you come here right this minute!"

74
00:04:34.521 --> 00:04:35.242
ordered Molly.

75
00:04:35.262 --> 00:04:37.064
"Ruff, ruff!"

76
00:04:37.344 --> 00:04:38.044
barked Bunch.

77
00:04:39.346 --> 00:04:41.487
But there was no sign of Caswell.

78
00:04:41.507 --> 00:04:46.552
"Caswell! Caswell, come back!"

79
00:04:47.092 --> 00:04:47.813
we shouted.

80
00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.136
We looked in the basement and up on the roof.

81
00:04:52.628 --> 00:04:57.632
We even looked in our tiny backyard, but all we saw was a cat.

82
00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:02.977
She was wearing a bell around her neck that tinkled whenever she walked.

83
00:05:04.418 --> 00:05:07.341
That was when I got my next brilliant idea!

84
00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:11.745
It would help us find Caswell whenever he got lost.

85
00:05:12.665 --> 00:05:15.028
It was the best idea I'd ever had.

86
00:05:16.409 --> 00:05:19.071
But first we needed to find Caswell!
